// The feature-area crosswalk: what a reader must be able to understand, each area mapped to the
// skills and commands that provide it and to the page that explains it.
//
// The sections under src/docs/ are the reading view; this file is the planning view beside it.
// `verify:features` holds the two together: every skill named here is in the vendored catalogue
// (src/_data/skillCatalogue.json5), every `page` named here exists under src/docs/, and every
// Markdown page in the Skills, Ways of working, Knowledge and Standards sections is claimed by
// exactly one area, Skills pages excepted because they are about skills in general rather than
// about one area. `partials/provided-by.njk` renders an area's skills and commands on the page it
// names, so the box a reader sees is derived from this file rather than typed on each page.
//
// Fields:
//   slug      the area's stable key, also the leaf of the page it will be explained on
//   title     how the area is named on the site
//   skills    the catalogue skills that provide it; a glob in the plan is written out in full here
//             so that every entry can be checked against the catalogue by name
//   commands  the `ki` command groups that provide it, as the reader would type them; may be empty
//   page      the site path of the page that explains the area, as a string or, where one area is
//             explained across more than one page, a list; omitted while the page does not exist
//   interim   true where the practice is written up before its standard home is chosen, so the page
//             is labelled interim throughout
//
// Order is the plan's order and carries no meaning on the site.

[
  {
    slug: 'the-work-model',
    title: 'The work model',
    skills: ['ki-coordination', 'ki-work-package'],
    commands: ['ki work status'],
    page: '/docs/ways-of-working/the-work-model/'
  },
  {
